[Music]  there are two special cases we need to  look at while finding the HCF and LCM of  two numbers first case when one number  is a multiple of the other and second  when they have no common factors except  one which means they are co-prime let's  understand the cases in detail the first  case would have numbers like four and  eight eight is a multiple of four or  numbers like 21 and 7 21 is a multiple  of seven one number is a multiple of the  other why is it a special case it's  because in such cases the LCM is always  the greater number the LCM of four and  eight will be eight and the LCM of 21  and seven will be 21 and the HCF will  always be the smaller number the HCF of  these two numbers will be 4 and the HCF  of these two numbers will be 7 what  about the second case an example of two  co-prime numbers would be 4 and 7 or 3 &amp;  5 both these pairs have no common  factors except one what is so special  about LCM and HCF of such numbers well  the LCM of such numbers will always  equal the product of the two numbers for  the first pair the LCM will be 4 times 7  which equals 28 and for the second pair  the LCM will equal 3 times 5 which  equals 15 and what will be the HCF of  such numbers it will always be 1 the 8  CF of 4 and 7 as well as the 8 CF of 3  and 5 equals 1 but  remember these techniques should be used  only to verify your answers  [Music]

